Hands-on Session: Monolayer Boron Nitride
===================================
:Author: Diana Y. Qiu, Felipe Jornada and David Strubbe
:Date: 2016/09/15


Overview
--------

In this session we will calculate the inverse dielectric matrix, quasiparticle band structure,
optical spectrum, and exciton wave functions of a monolayer of BN using GW-BSE.


Goals
-----

The basic goals are the following:

  1. Run a basic GW-BSE calculation for a 2D semiconductor.
  2. Understand the effect of Coulomb truncation on the inverse dielectric matrix.
  3. Understand the meaning of the head of the dielectric matrix in 2D.
  4. Demonstrate how to calculate absorption spectrum and excitonic wave functions for a 
     2D semiconductor.


Instruction
-----------

1. Go to the ``1-mf/`` directory, where we perform all the mean-field
   calculations. Follow the steps in the README file to generate the various
   wavefunctions.

2. Go to the ``2-bgw/`` directory, where we perform GW/GW-BSE calculations.
   Follow the instructions in the README file to perform the GW/GW-BSE
   calculations.
